  "notes": "Compound of {工事|こうじ} (construction work) + {中|ちゅう} (in the middle of). Very commonly seen on signs at construction sites, roads, and buildings in Japan.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {工事中|こうじちゅう}のため: due to construction\n- {道路|どうろ}{工事中|こうじちゅう}: road under construction\n- ただいま{工事中|こうじちゅう}: currently under construction\n\nSIMILAR 〜{中|ちゅう} EXPRESSIONS:\n- {清掃中|せいそうちゅう}: cleaning in progress\n- {点検中|てんけんちゅう}: under inspection\n- {使用中|しようちゅう}: in use\n- {故障中|こしょうちゅう}: out of order\n- {準備中|じゅんびちゅう}: preparing\n\nThe 〜{中|ちゅう} suffix attaches to action nouns to indicate that the action is currently ongoing.",
